  REMARK    STRUCTURE BY ELECTRON MICROSCOPY (3.00 ANGSTROMS) OF 24-398 IN
            COMPLEX WITH UCN; GNB1; GNG2 AND GNAS, FUNCTION, AND MUTAGENESIS OF
            232-ILE--TRP-236 AND 251-LEU--TRP-259.
COMMENT     On May 31, 2024 this sequence version replaced P34998.1.
            [FUNCTION] G protein-coupled receptor for CRH and UCN stress
            hormones, which plays a central role in whole body adaptation to
            stress (PubMed:18292205, PubMed:18801728, PubMed:20966082,
            PubMed:23576434, PubMed:23863939, PubMed:24290358, PubMed:32004469,
            PubMed:32004470). Ligand binding causes a conformation change that
            triggers signaling via guanine nucleotide-binding proteins (G
            proteins) and downstream effectors, such as adenylate cyclase
            (PubMed:18292205, PubMed:32004469, PubMed:32004470). CRHR1 is
            mainly coupled to G(s) G protein (GNAS), mediating activation of
            adenylate cyclase activity and production of cAMP (PubMed:18292205,
            PubMed:32004469, PubMed:32004470). In some conditions, can also
            couple to G(q) G protein (GNAQ) and mediate production of
            diacylglycerol (DAG) and inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate (IP3) second
            messengers (PubMed:14657255). CRHR1-dependent signaling is a
            primary mediator of the neuroendocrine, autonomic (fight-or-flight)
            and behavioral responses to stress, acting as a key regulator of
            adaptation by activating the hypothalamus-pituitary-adrenal axis,
            leading to corticotropin hormone (ACTH) production (By similarity).
            Mediates both anxiogenic and anxiolytic response to stress in
            glutamatergic and dopaminergic neurons, respectively (By
            similarity). CRHR1 also plays a critical role in addiction by
            mediating the brain's stress response, particularly during
            withdrawal and relapse: it drives the transition to compulsive drug
            seeking by increasing anxiety and negative emotional states (By
            similarity). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P35347,
            ECO:0000269|PubMed:14657255, ECO:0000269|PubMed:18292205,
            ECO:0000269|PubMed:18801728, ECO:0000269|PubMed:20966082,
            ECO:0000269|PubMed:23576434, ECO:0000269|PubMed:23863939,
            ECO:0000269|PubMed:24290358, ECO:0000269|PubMed:32004469,
            ECO:0000269|PubMed:32004470}.
            [FUNCTION] [Isoform CRF-R3]: Does not bind to CRH with high
            affinity. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:7811272}.
            [SUBUNIT] Heterodimer; heterodimerizes with GPER1 (By similarity).
            Interacts with DLG1; this inhibits endocytosis of CRHR1 after
            agonist binding (PubMed:23576434). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P35353,
            ECO:0000269|PubMed:23576434}.
            [INTERACTION] P34998; Q02410: APBA1; NbExp=2; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-368690; P34998; Q99767: APBA2; NbExp=2; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-81711; P34998; P06850: CRH; NbExp=5; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-3870390; P34998; Q12959: DLG1; NbExp=4; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-357481; P34998; Q15700: DLG2; NbExp=2; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-80426; P34998; Q92796: DLG3; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-80440; P34998; P78352: DLG4; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-80389; P34998; Q68DX3: FRMPD2; NbExp=2; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-53993476; P34998; A4D2P6: GRID2IP; NbExp=2; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-15893226; P34998; Q9Y3R0: GRIP1; NbExp=5; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-5349621; P34998; Q9C0E4: GRIP2; NbExp=5; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-949557; P34998; Q14005: IL16; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-2831580; P34998; Q8TBB1: LNX1; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-739832; P34998; Q8N448: LNX2; NbExp=2; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-2340947; P34998; Q96QZ7: MAGI1; NbExp=2; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-924464; P34998; Q86UL8: MAGI2; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-311035; P34998; O75970: MPDZ; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-821405; P34998; Q8NI35: PATJ; NbExp=7; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-724390; P34998; Q5T2W1: PDZK1; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-349819; P34998; O60895: RAMP2; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-9009040; P34998; O60896: RAMP3; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-720447; P34998; Q14160: SCRIB; NbExp=5; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-357345; P34998; Q07157: TJP1; NbExp=2; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-79553; P34998; Q9P202: WHRN; NbExp=3; IntAct=EBI-3870393,
            EBI-310886; P34998; Q63622: Dlg2; Xeno; NbExp=2;
            IntAct=EBI-3870393, EBI-396947; P34998; O88382: Magi2; Xeno;
            NbExp=2; IntAct=EBI-3870393, EBI-696179.
            [SUBCELLULAR LOCATION] Cell membrane {ECO:0000269|PubMed:18292205};
            Multi-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000269|PubMed:32004469,
            ECO:0000269|PubMed:32004470}. Note=Agonist-binding promotes
            endocytosis. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:23576434}.
            [ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS] Event=Alternative splicing; Named
            isoforms=5; Name=CRF-R2; IsoId=P34998-2; Sequence=Displayed;
            Name=CRF-R1; IsoId=P34998-1; Sequence=VSP_062278; Name=CRF-R3;
            IsoId=P34998-3; Sequence=VSP_062277; Name=CRF-R4; Synonyms=1D;
            IsoId=P34998-4; Sequence=VSP_062279; Name=5; IsoId=P34998-5;
            Sequence=VSP_062276.
            [TISSUE SPECIFICITY] Predominantly expressed in the cerebellum,
            pituitary, cerebral cortex and olfactory lobe.
            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:8243652}.
            [DOMAIN] The transmembrane domain is composed of seven
            transmembrane helices that are arranged in V-shape
            (PubMed:23863939). Transmembrane helix 7 assumes a sharply kinked
            structure (PubMed:23863939). The antagonist CP-376395 binds at an
            allosteric site, far from the presumed binding site for the
            physiological peptide ligand (PubMed:23863939).
            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:23863939}.
            [PTM] C-terminal Ser or Thr residues may be phosphorylated
            (PubMed:14657255). Phosphorylation at Ser-301 by PKA prevents
            maximal coupling to Gq-protein, and thereby negatively regulates
            downstream signaling (PubMed:14657255).
            {ECO:0000269|PubMed:14657255}.
            [MISCELLANEOUS] [Isoform CRF-R2]: Major isoform. {ECO:0000305}.
            [SIMILARITY] Belongs to the G protein-coupled receptor 2 family.
            {ECO:0000305}.
